RoboEyes-style face on bread-compact-wifi-lcd (GC9A01)
=========================================================

The GC9A01 build of this board draws a two-eye face on the single 240x240
round panel. That face is an original RGB565 renderer written for this
repository (`roboeyes_face.cc` / `roboeyes_display.cc`). It is not a copy or
mechanical translation of FluxGarage/RoboEyes, and this tree does not vendor
that project's source or the Adafruit GFX library it depends on.

The on-screen look — two cyan eyes on a black round screen, a fast blink,
idle glances, and simple happy / angry / tired shapes — is inspired by
FluxGarage RoboEyes:

  https://github.com/FluxGarage/RoboEyes
  Copyright (c) FluxGarage
  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only

RoboEyes is GPL-3.0-only. Adafruit GFX, which RoboEyes builds on, is
BSD-3-Clause. Because those sources are not linked into this firmware, the
rest of this repository stays under the MIT license in the top-level LICENSE
file. Do not drop the original RoboEyes sources into this tree without
treating the combined work as GPL-3.0.

No Anki, Cozmo, or other non-free face assets are included. The eyes are
drawn at runtime. No emoji pack is required for the face.
